      "content": "Shinkansen trains have designated luggage areas, particularly in the vestibules, but keeping bulky gear strictly in those spots is best for smooth travel. If your equipment is extremely large, consider shipping it ahead via luggage forwarding services between cities. For smaller, necessary items, use the train's overhead racks or dedicated luggage racks in the quieter cars to avoid clogging aisles at busy stations. This preparation minimizes strain during crowded boarding and alighting.",
